{"animath":"0.1","canvas":{"height":540,"width":960},"kind":"concept","level":"secondary","scenes":[{"caption":"A mole is a counting word","duration_ms":8000,"id":"s1","narration":"Chemists count particles in moles, the same way a baker counts eggs in dozens. One dozen is 12 items. One mole is 6.02 × 10 to the 23rd items — that is Avogadro's number.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"A mole is a counting word","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dozL","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"1 dozen eggs = 12 eggs","x":80,"y":160}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":110,"cy":220,"fill":"#f5cba7","id":"egg1","kind":"circle","r":16,"stroke":"#8e5a2b","width":2}},{"at_ms":1050,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":150,"cy":220,"fill":"#f5cba7","id":"egg2","kind":"circle","r":16,"stroke":"#8e5a2b","width":2}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":190,"cy":220,"fill":"#f5cba7","id":"egg3","kind":"circle","r":16,"stroke":"#8e5a2b","width":2}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":230,"cy":220,"fill":"#f5cba7","id":"egg4","kind":"circle","r":16,"stroke":"#8e5a2b","width":2}},{"at_ms":1700,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dotL","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"… × 3 rows = 12","x":280,"y":232}},{"at_ms":2400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"moleL","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"1 mole of particles = 6.02 × 10²³ particles","x":80,"y":330}},{"at_ms":3100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"avoL","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"Avogadro's number","x":80,"y":380}},{"at_ms":3700,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tooBig","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"far too many to count one by one","x":80,"y":430}},{"at_ms":4600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"so","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"…so we weigh moles instead of counting atoms.","x":80,"y":480}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"caption","text":"A mole is just a number — a very large one."}]},{"caption":"Mass to moles: the formula","duration_ms":9000,"id":"s2","narration":"The mass of one mole of carbon-12 is 12 grams — that is its molar mass. Moles equal mass divided by molar mass. So 12 grams of carbon is exactly 1 mole.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Mass to moles","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"formula","kind":"latex","size":40,"tex":"n = \\frac{m}{M}","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legend","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"n = moles,  m = mass,  M = molar mass","x":80,"y":260}},{"at_ms":2000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"given","kind":"text","size":26,"text":"We have 12 g of carbon. M = 12 g/mol.","x":80,"y":340}},{"at_ms":2900,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"work","kind":"latex","size":36,"tex":"n = \\frac{12\\ \\text{g}}{12\\ \\text{g/mol}} = 1\\ \\text{mol}","x":80,"y":420}},{"at_ms":4200,"do":"emphasize","target":"work"},{"at_ms":5000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"t1","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"Grams cancel. The answer is in moles.","x":80,"y":500}},{"at_ms":6400,"do":"caption","text":"Mass ÷ molar mass = moles. Units check the maths."}]},{"caption":"Mole ratios in reactions","duration_ms":8500,"id":"s3","narration":"Balanced equations count moles, not grams. Two moles of hydrogen react with one mole of oxygen to make two moles of water. So 4 moles of hydrogen need 2 moles of oxygen.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Mole ratios","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"eqn","kind":"text","size":32,"text":"2 H₂ + O₂ → 2 H₂O","x":80,"y":160}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ratio","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"moles:  2   :  1   :  2","x":80,"y":220}},{"at_ms":2000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"q","kind":"text","size":26,"text":"How much O₂ for 4 mol of H₂?","x":80,"y":310}},{"at_ms":2800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"scale","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#1f7a3a","width":4,"x1":120,"x2":560,"y1":370,"y2":370}},{"at_ms":3100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"scaleL","kind":"text","size":22,"text":"double everything","x":640,"y":382}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ans","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"2 mol H₂ : 1 mol O₂  →  4 mol H₂ : 2 mol O₂","x":80,"y":440}},{"at_ms":5200,"do":"emphasize","target":"ans"},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"caption","text":"Scale every coefficient by the same factor."}]},{"caption":"Check the thinking","duration_ms":6500,"id":"s4","narration":"One mole is a number, not a mass. One mole of carbon weighs 12 grams, but one mole of water weighs 18 grams — same number of particles, different mass per particle.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Check the thinking","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"myth","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"❌ “1 mol = 1 gram.”","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":300,"cy":300,"fill":"#1a1a1a","id":"cAtom","kind":"circle","r":26,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":2}},{"at_ms":1700,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"cL","kind":"text","size":22,"text":"1 mol of C = 12 g","x":220,"y":360}},{"at_ms":2400,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":620,"cy":300,"fill":"#2471a3","id":"wAtom","kind":"circle","r":26,"stroke":"#2471a3","width":2}},{"at_ms":2600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"wL","kind":"text","size":22,"text":"1 mol of H₂O = 18 g","x":530,"y":360}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fix","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"Same number of particles. Different mass.","x":80,"y":450}},{"at_ms":4700,"do":"caption","text":"1 mol is a count — the mass depends on the particle."}]}],"subject":"science","title":"The mole: counting atoms by weighing","topic":"chem-mole"}